    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "24d4cef1_110b30c4",
        "filename": "include/ec_commands.h",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 4227,
      "author": {
        "id": 1003000
      },
      "writtenOn": "2019-03-09T02:35:39Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I was thinking about this some more today and was wondering if it would be cleaner to put this in a union of its own indicating what sleep event the param is applicable for.\n\ni.e.\n\nunion {\n    /* Params for HOST_SLEEP_EVENT_S0IX_SUSPEND */\n    struct s0ix_params {\n         uint16_t s0ix_timeout;\n    };\n    uint16_t reserved;\n};\n\nSimilary for response below. That keeps it very clear when the param is valid and when it is just reserved.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 4227,
        "startChar": 2,
        "endLine": 4227,
        "endChar": 3
      },
      "revId": "253c752214d1b9c2b8878431940b26a6acc178da",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "30cf1e4d_e574bfb2",
        "filename": "include/ec_commands.h",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 4227,
      "author": {
        "id": 1260470
      },
      "writtenOn": "2019-03-11T16:30:00Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I\u0027d actually like to avoid mentioning s0ix in the protocol section, at least outside of comments. I\u0027m trying to keep this facility generic from the protocol perspective. The fact that it\u0027s only currently implemented for S0ix is an implementation detail, not a protocol detail. I imagine others in the future may want to wire this functionality up for other sleep lines. For instance, we have this exact same problem for S3 in Cheza, where if the bus votes aren\u0027t all correct then it suspends to a shallower idle state and just quietly doesn\u0027t do full power collapse.",
      "parentUuid": "24d4cef1_110b30c4",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 4227,
        "startChar": 2,
        "endLine": 4227,
        "endChar": 3
      },
      "revId": "253c752214d1b9c2b8878431940b26a6acc178da",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "70ef368b_80bd8eea",
        "filename": "include/ec_commands.h",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 4227,
      "author": {
        "id": 1003000
      },
      "writtenOn": "2019-03-11T17:47:16Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Taking the example of MKBP event command/response:\n\nhttps://chromium.googlesource.com/chromiumos/platform/ec/+/refs/heads/master/include/ec_commands.h#3464\n\nhttps://chromium.googlesource.com/chromiumos/platform/ec/+/refs/heads/master/include/ec_commands.h#3439\n\nI understand the case for EC_CMD_HOST_SLEEP_EVENT is slightly different because these are maybe more related than MKBP events, but if we look closely at the sleep event types, then the command params/response do not apply to every event.\n\ne.g. timeout in command: Applies to HOST_SLEEP_EVENT_S0IX_SUSPEND. Could be extended to HOST_SLEEP_EVENT_S3_SUSPEND and HOST_SLEEP_EVENT_S3_WAKEABLE_SUSPEND. Does not apply to HOST_SLEEP_EVENT_S3_RESUME or HOST_SLEEP_EVENT_S0IX_RESUME.\n\nSimilarly on the response side -- sleep_transitions -- Applies to HOST_SLEEP_EVENT_S3_RESUME and HOST_SLEEP_EVENT_S0IX_RESUME, but does not apply to other sleep event types (HOST_SLEEP_EVENT_S0IX_SUSPEND, HOST_SLEEP_EVENT_S3_SUSPEND, HOST_SLEEP_EVENT_S3_WAKEABLE_SUSPEND). Hence, the ask to make the params separate and apply only to specific event types.\n\nIf you want, you can have suspend_params and resume_resp_params. But since it is a union, I don\u0027t think it saves/consumes more/less space. But helps with the clarity, especially because this file is included by multiple users -- kernel, coreboot, depthcharge (though kernel is the only user of this specific command).",
      "parentUuid": "30cf1e4d_e574bfb2",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 4227,
        "startChar": 2,
        "endLine": 4227,
        "endChar": 3
      },
      "revId": "253c752214d1b9c2b8878431940b26a6acc178da",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": true
    },
