    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "ab675896_c26390ee",
        "filename": "power/intel_x86.c",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 252,
      "author": {
        "id": 1003000
      },
      "writtenOn": "2019-03-09T02:35:39Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Why is the count incremented on both suspend and resume? Wouldn\u0027t it be better to just increment on suspend. Allows holding double the number of entries than sleep signal transitions.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 252,
        "startChar": 1,
        "endLine": 252,
        "endChar": 29
      },
      "revId": "253c752214d1b9c2b8878431940b26a6acc178da",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "78f4df54_f4926165",
        "filename": "power/intel_x86.c",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 252,
      "author": {
        "id": 1260470
      },
      "writtenOn": "2019-03-11T16:30:00Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "This is a debugging facility, I\u0027d rather not make assumptions like that. Maybe the sleep line is storming and toggling too fast for the EC to notice, (or maybe the EC gets way too bogged down and is missing transitions). It seems most useful to faithfully report what was seen, rather than baking in assumptions. Are you worried that we\u0027ll do more than 32000 transitions during a sleep phase, and then detect a problem we\u0027ll want to look into? I could extend the counter out to 32-bits.",
      "parentUuid": "ab675896_c26390ee",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 252,
        "startChar": 1,
        "endLine": 252,
        "endChar": 29
      },
      "revId": "253c752214d1b9c2b8878431940b26a6acc178da",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "04a258c0_2aad5170",
        "filename": "power/intel_x86.c",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 252,
