      "side": 1,
      "message": "\u003e This is a debugging facility, I\u0027d rather not make assumptions like that. Maybe the sleep \n\u003e line is storming and toggling too fast for the EC to notice, (or maybe the EC gets way too \n\u003e bogged down and is missing transitions).\n\nI don\u0027t understand the comment about assumptions. Isn\u0027t it safe to assume that if the SLP_S0# line was asserted, it would be de-asserted only once before it is asserted again? If there is a storm that keeps the EC from noticing, then there is actually no good way for even incrementing this count i.e. the count is anyways not going to be accurate. So, it is still best-effort.\n\n\u003e Are you worried that we\u0027ll do more than 32000 transitions during a sleep phase, and then \n\u003e detect a problem we\u0027ll want to look into?\n\nThat is actually very much possible. On KBL, SLP_S0# toggles every 8 seconds (1 de-assertion and 1 assertion). With that it takes ~2048 seconds to reach ~32000 transitions (2048 * 8 * 2), which is ~30minutes of sleep. Bumping up to 32 definitely sounds like a good thing to do.",
